QED for gem4xe -- what the program is made of, and on what terms
=================================================================

QED.PRG is one program linked from four parts.  Each keeps its own terms.

1. QED
   https://github.com/freemint/qed

   Written by Tom Quellenberg; maintained by Christian Felsch (3.20-4.53),
   Heiko Achilles (5.0-5.0.2) and the FreeMiNT project since 2002.  From
   version 3.09, in the author's words (dist/liesmich.txt, October 1994):
   QED including its sources is public domain.  Anyone may have the
   sources, change them and publish changed versions.  What the author
   forbids is distributing the sources or the program for a fee of any
   kind.

   The gem4xe port's own files are under the same terms.

   SO THIS PROGRAM MAY BE GIVEN AWAY, BUT NOT SOLD, alone or as part of
   anything else.

2. The gem4xe application kit
   https://github.com/slaapliedje/gem4xe

   The start-up code and GEM bindings every gem4xe program links.
   GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or (at your option) any
   later version; the text is COPYING.LIB, beside this file.  Its source
   is in the gem4xe repository (src/app/, src/portab.h).  This port's
   source, which is what the LGPL needs to let you relink QED against a
   changed kit, is this directory.

3. cflib
   https://github.com/freemint/cflib

   The ST application library QED uses.  GNU Lesser General Public
   License, version 2.1 or later (COPYING.LIB).  Linked unmodified.

4. The Calypsi C library, from Apache NuttX
   https://nuttx.apache.org/

   The standard C functions QED calls -- stdio, printf and scanf, the
   string and number conversions -- come from the Calypsi C library,
   which is derived from Apache NuttX and modified for Calypsi by Hakan
   Thorngren.  Apache License, Version 2.0; the text is
   LICENSE-APACHE-2.0, beside this file.

